    {
      "id": "claim_0b928306c4b84e1192919ad58ce2adcc",
      "statement": "The common bootstrap path creates an insecure CA client (no root exists yet), fetches the root certificate by fingerprint via client.Root which validates it, creates/activates a context or prints the contexts advisory, writes the root (0600) and defaults.json (0644) with the CA URL normalized to https, optionally creates the profile defaults file, and with --install installs the root into the system truststore; no local state is written if the root fetch/verification fails.",
